{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>For an abomination to YHWH is everyone who does these.</b> Any one of these nine that were mentioned. <b>And because of these abominations.</b> — that they made abominable with them YHWH your Elohim, who is exalted above all wisdomes and constellations, who turns the sphere and confounds the constellations, to dispossess them from before you; and this is the sense of בגלל. And so our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded concerning charity (Deuteronomy 15:10): ״כי בגלל הדבר הזה״ — גלגל הוא שחוזר בעולם (it is a wheel that turns in the world). Therefore you must abhor everything that the Holy One, blessed be He, abhors; and since these things are an abomination before Him, you must take care not to engage in them and that your heart not be drawn after them, but rather that you be whole in the service of the Name, may He be exalted. This is what it says: ״תמים תהיה עם ה' אלהיך״ — whole shall you be with YHWH your Elohim — that is, let your heart be whole in fear of Him, to do what He commanded and to guard against what He forbade. And the meaning of תמים is that one's inside be as one's outside, and that he be upright in his speech and in his deeds. And I have already mentioned this in connection with the verse (Genesis 17): ״והיה תמים״. And ״תמים תהיה עם ה' אלהיך״ further includes: if you are whole, you will be עם ה' אלהיך — with YHWH your Elohim — in the manner of Moses (Exodus 34:28): ״ויהי שם עם ה'״, and likewise concerning the supernal Light (Daniel 2:22): ״ונהורא עמיה שרא״. And this verse teaches you about the excellence of the quality of wholeness (temimut) and about the greatness of its reward, as David, peace be upon him, said (Psalms 41:13): ״ואני בתומי תמכתי בי ותציבני לפניך לעולם״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:49:19.703139365Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}